&#x000f3;n Lagunera, Mexico</article-title><source>Food Chem Toxicol</source><volume>40</volume><fpage>1423</fpage><lpage>1431</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12387304</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ehp0115-001371"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group><name><surname>Detterman</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name></person-group><year>1988</year><source>Cognitive Abilities Test</source><publisher-loc>Cleveland, OH</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Case Western University</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b17-ehp0115-001371"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diawara</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Litt</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Unis</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Alfonso</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Martinez</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Crock</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Arsenic, cadmium, lead, and mercury in surface soils, Pueblo, Colorado: implications for population health risk</article-title><source>Environ Geochem Health</source><volume>28</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>297</fpage><lpage>315</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16752202</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18-ehp0115-001371"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diaz-Barriga</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Batres</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Calder&#x000f3;n</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lugo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Galvao</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lara</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Rizo</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><a